{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/82447-demon-stigmatics","id":82447,"title":"Demon Stigmatics","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-01T19:01:54-08:00","id":82447,"title":"Demon Stigmatics","content":"So one thing a friend of mine was pointing out was that Stigmatics seem to be the least supernatural of the lesser supernatural templates, and that while the Supernatural merits are cool, they aren't <i>that </i>great.<br /> <br /> Which is sort of the point, right?<br /> <br /> Anyway, we're thinking we want to play a Demon game, but one of the players doesn't want to play a Demon but rather they want to play a Stigmatic. Their concern is that as the team stigmatic, they might turn out to be dead weight in the midst of a group of badass awesome demons.<br /> <br /> Now, while I might be thinking that's the price you pay for playing a mortal, I do want to meet my player halfway here. I think it's been mentioned that the Player's Guide might have something to this effect, but it's worth asking: What would you do to Stigmatics specifically working for Demons? Do you think they might learn how to use Embeds?<br /> <br /> What sort of hotfixes might you propose? What can I do to make the Stigmatic experience a more interesting one?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T19:21:28-08:00","id":82451,"title":"","content":"Merit dots for Gadgets springs to mind immediately, but I feel it's worth pointing out that having powers that trigger neither compromise nor aetheric resonance is nothing to sneeze at in a game of techgnostic espionage, nor is the ability to suppress one's stigmata in comparison to the Unchained's inability to do the same to their glitches.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T19:29:01-08:00","id":82455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/82447-demon-stigmatics?p=82451#post82451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Merit dots for Gadgets springs to mind immediately, but I feel it's worth pointing out that having powers that trigger neither compromise nor aetheric resonance is nothing to sneeze at in a game of techgnostic espionage, nor is the ability to suppress one's stigmata in comparison to the Unchained's inability to do the same to their glitches.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which reminds me, You can import the entire Inspector Gadget cartoon series into a Demon game and have it work just fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T19:41:25-08:00","id":82459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/82447-demon-stigmatics?p=82451#post82451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Merit dots for Gadgets springs to mind immediately, but I feel it's worth pointing out that having powers that trigger neither compromise nor aetheric resonance is nothing to sneeze at in a game of techgnostic espionage, nor is the ability to suppress one's stigmata in comparison to the Unchained's inability to do the same to their glitches.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, my initial thought was that they should be able to get Embeds, but the lack of compromise for mortals is awkward.<br /> <br /> A thought that occurs to me is that they might make a compromise roll and risk getting some of the Conditions that demons can get but the other thing is that I'm not sure those are entirely applicable.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T20:01:00-08:00","id":82468,"title":"","content":"Offer the player extra merit points at character creation. Give him an extra beat per session. There's a whole slew of merits available in the GMC, and even (a little adjusting maybe) Second Sight. Roleplaying wise, Stigmatics are also used by the God-Machine and it's Angels. So now your Demon's can have a double agent. A perfect man inside. There's tons of things this character can do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T04:29:47-08:00","id":82584,"title":"","content":"Well, here's the thing about Stigmatics. And ghouls, for that matter. They have a place in Demon (or Vamp) society, yes. Usually as a lesser one; part of the appeal of playing a lesser template is that you are mortal still, dealing with forces beyond your complete comprehension and power. But they also can function in roles that pretty much the supernaturals cannot. What does that mean, you ask?<br /> <br /> Ghouls are the daylight servants of the Kindred. They go out and do things, be their loyal eyes and ears when they cannot. They also often serve as Touchstones for Kindred, keeping them sane and, well, human. Stigmatics, on the other hand, are still connected to the God Machine. Well, as much as any mortal is. They can get information and visions of what the God Machine is doing that demons can't. Not even by Embeds or Exploits.<br /> <br /> After that? Have the PCs make some Gadgets for him? A Hellfire gun is handy to have, along with a Merciless Gunman scope.<br /> <br /> And then, Pact. Stigmatics still qualify for bonuses from pacts. Which, given Descent's options, can be heavily weighted towards the mortal instead of the other way. That's a bit of nice bonus right there.<br /> <br /> And, lack of Compromise for mortals? That's a feature of being a lesser template, not a bug. Part of the whole point is being able to do things without the drawbacks. Well, they tend to come with their own drawbacks. Ghouls get addiction, Stigmatics get Spooked and another condition. But, still! Stigmatics can do things in a &quot;vulgar&quot; way that Demons can't without losing Cover. That means they can be more reckless or obvious. That alone makes them far more useful than you'd think. <br /> <br /> Hells. Give the Stigmatic an embeded Gadget with the ability to get information from machines. He could do that all he wants without risking Cover. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It sounds like that the player just doesn't want to be overshadowed by demons, who can do everything he can, but potentially better. The best way to offset this is to 1) play up the visions, 2) let him stand out in situations and do things where everyone else would be hampered by Compromise rolls, and most importantly 3) arrange a niche between him and the other players. If he doesn't want to be overshadowed... then the best way to do that is for him to have a skill set and ability set that no one else does. Honestly, this last one is probably the most important one. Not being overshadowed and rendered redundant is probably the most important thing. So, work to make sure that happens.<br /> <br /> No need for special rules or anything along those lines. Just... &quot;no one else can do X, and you've got enough tricks to be able to play along in combat or social or investigation scenes as well.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Offer the player extra merit points at character creation. </div> </div> </div> They automatically start with 3 more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 03-02-2014, 07:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T07:46:15-08:00","id":82626,"title":"","content":"Do they? I must have read that rule and it slipped my mine between now in then. Jolly Good. Not like I don't plan on reading the book again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T07:49:17-08:00","id":82631,"title":"","content":"One should also not underestimate the usefulness of playing a character that can act as an early warning system for the party. Stigmatics' special Omen sense could allow the player to just know things where the Machine is concerned. I think it could work fine, the player would just have to be comfortable with having less raw power.<br /> <br /> -Slag","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T11:15:50-08:00","id":82703,"title":"","content":"Thank you guys. You've really helped me come up with how I want to play this, and I think I'm going to put emphasis on the Omen Sensitivity as an early warning system and the use of the supernatural merits as investigative tools.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T14:08:25-08:00","id":82773,"title":"","content":"Glad to help","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}